{"id": 54, "ts": 1783858440.3011365, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I agree with Agent\u202f1 that Candidate\u202fB remains the strongest option given the concrete evidence we have\u2014his conscientiousness, excellent stress handling, and solid weather\u2011assessment skills directly support the reliability and calmness needed for long\u2011distance flights. However, we still lack decisive data on Candidate\u202fD\u2019s decision quality in safety\u2011critical moments and his actual crew\u2011cooperation behavior; the notes only mention he \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately\u201d and \u201csolves problems extremely well,\u201d which are promising but not sufficient to assess his safety\u2011critical decision making. Until we can confirm that D can consistently make high\u2011quality decisions under pressure and work constructively with the crew, B\u2019s proven strengths keep him ahead. Therefore, I maintain my provisional vote for **Candidate\u202fB**."}
